      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see what you did there. It's definitely longer now, but to be honest, it feels a bit repetitive. You're basically just rephrasing the same sentences with more \"corporate speak,\" which doesn't actually make the guide more useful for an engineer in a hurry. \n\nThe audit score is still hovering in the red, though. If we can get the word count up by adding some actual substance—like a \"Troubleshooting\" section for common error codes or a more detailed \"Deep Dive\" into the configuration parameters—it might satisfy the metric while actually being helpful. Can you try one more version that hits a much higher word count through actual added technical detail or comprehensive context? Just don't lose the professional tone.",
